hings temper that.\n  - Data-centre grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027, which is slower than 2026.\n  - Utility spending depends on financing.\n  - The demand figures support the bullish case. Pellham Power plans 2027 capex up 18%, including a transformer tender of about C$900M due to award in Q1 2027. VLTX utility order intake was C$670M in 2026Q3.\n- **Financing (n3):** Debt markets are mostly open, but equity markets are not reliable.\n  - Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp.\n  - Two utility share offerings were cut back in Q3.\n  - Pellham, the largest spender, is the weak point. It was placed on negative watch after withdrawing an offering.\n  - Funding risk is therefore concentrated in the customer behind the biggest tender, and the Q1 2027 award could slip or shrink.\n- **Pricing (n4):** The LEAPS look fairly priced.\n  - Implied volatility is 27% against a 2-year median of 26%.\n  - The Jan-2029 implied volatility is 27.5%.\n  - There is no pricing edge, so adding doesn't pay off on cheap options.\n\n**Suggested approach:** Demand supports a long position, but fair pricing gives no discount and financing risk is clustered around the Pellham tender. A reasonable plan is to add a small tranche now, then add more after the Q1 2027 award or once equity and credit conditions improve. That wait costs little because implied volatility is not cheap.\n\nThis is analysis, not personalised financial advice. Check position size and strikes against your own risk limits.","ttft_ms":2931,"type":"result","duration_ms":49420,"uuid":"2a72f5b4-1750-4de6-b588-5cf01cc4269d","ttft_stream_ms":2250,"time_to_request_ms":132,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":10,"system_prompt":6,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":5,"input_attachments":19,"input_hooks":6,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":7,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":9,"init_frame_send":5,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":8,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":